+# NoctiNIRS fNIRS validation firmware
+
+Target: ESP32-S3, ESP-IDF 5.5.1.
+
+The active application is `main/app_main_fnirs_test.c`. This revision implements protocol `paired_v2`, where every 100 ms optical frame is transmitted as two phase records with the same `frame_id`:
+
+```text
+LED-ON phase  +  LED-OFF phase
+               |
+               v
+I_corrected = I_LED_ON - I_LED_OFF
+```
+
+`I_LED_OFF` means LED-off intensity. It may contain photodiode dark current, electronic offset, ambient light, and other LED-off contributions.
+
+## Precision timing
+
+```text
+ADS131M04 data rate       4000 SPS (250 us/sample)
+Optical frame rate        10 Hz
+Slots per frame           20
+Slot period               5000 us
+LED-ON settling guard     1000 us
+LED-ON sample window      1400 us
+LED-ON total budget       2400 us
+LED-OFF nominal budget    2600 us
+LED-OFF settling guard    1000 us
+Samples per phase         K=5 contiguous CRC-valid samples
+```
+
+The ADC runs continuously. The firmware does not retry a CRC-failed conversion by reading the next frame. For each phase, it accepts only the newest contiguous block of exactly five valid DRDY conversions after the settling guard. It never fills a missing sample using an older conversion.
+
+## Protocol behavior
+
+- Frame payload version: `2`
+- `NOCTI_FNIRS_FRAME_F_PAIRED`: phase belongs to paired acquisition
+- `NOCTI_FNIRS_FRAME_F_LED_OFF`: phase is LED-OFF; absence means LED-ON
+- Both phase records use the same `frame_id`
+- A slot is invalid when either phase is under-K, CRC-invalid, or missing
+- The host must never substitute an LED-OFF phase from another frame
+
+## Modes
+
+- `SCAN`: all 20 source/wavelength slots operate normally
+- `SINGLE`: only the selected slot lights; useful for validation
+- `DARK`: all LEDs intentionally remain off; diagnostic mode only
+
+Normal acquisition must start in `SCAN` or `SINGLE`. A separate five-second DARK session is no longer required.
+
+## Build and flash
+
+```bash
+idf.py fullclean
+idf.py build
+idf.py flash monitor
+```
+
+## Acceptance checks
+
+At boot:
+
+```text
+ADS131 DRDY count over 1 second: 3800..4200
+ADS131=4000 SPS
+paired K(on/off)=5/5
+```
+
+During a stable SCAN run, `STATUS` should show:
+
+```text
+protocol=paired_v2
+adc_sps=4000
+k_on=5 k_off=5
+min_n_on=5 min_n_off=5
+underk_on=0 underk_off=0
+partial=0
+crc_bad=0 led_err=0
+sched_missed=0 sched_abort=0
+```
+
+The measured `off_dark_min_us` must be greater than the 1000 us LED-OFF settling guard and should normally be near the nominal dark budget after I2C overhead.
+
+See `PAIRED_LED_OFF_V2.md` and `REVISION_NOTES_2026-07-17.md` for the design rationale and change list.
