+# Host handling for paired LED-OFF protocol v2
+
+1. Decode both fNIRS phase records.
+2. Key pending records by `UDP session_id + fNIRS frame_id`.
+3. Require one `led_on` and one `led_off` record.
+4. Validate each slot independently:
+   - valid bit set in both phases;
+   - no under-K bit;
+   - no CRC-drop bit;
+   - equal ON/OFF sample count;
+   - exact configured K when config v2 is available;
+   - four finite PD averages.
+5. Calculate signed corrected intensity for valid slots only.
+6. Expire unmatched phases; never use a previous frame as a fallback.
+
+The firmware currently uses K=5 at 4 kSPS with 1000 us settling guards for both phases. The bridge reads these values from the v2 config record rather than hard-coding them. If the config packet has not yet arrived, the firmware under-K masks remain authoritative and ON/OFF counts must still be equal.
